.Dd July 29, 2026
.Dt LIBFILESYSTEMCMP 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm libfilesystemcmp
.Nd public client transport for FileSystemCmp providers
.Sh LIBRARY
.Lb libfilesystemcmp
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In filesystemcmp.h
.Ft int
.Fn filesystemcmp_open "const char *component"
.Ft int
.Fn filesystemcmp_open_root "int fd" "struct filesystemcmp_handle *root"
.Ft int
.Fn filesystemcmp_lookup "int fd" "struct filesystemcmp_handle directory" "const char *name" "struct filesystemcmp_handle_reply *reply"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn filesystemcmp_pread "int fd" "struct filesystemcmp_handle object" "void *buffer" "size_t length" "uint64_t offset"
.Ft ssize_t
.Fn filesystemcmp_pwrite "int fd" "struct filesystemcmp_handle object" "const void *buffer" "size_t length" "uint64_t offset"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
library defines the provider-neutral
.Dv org.5bsd.cmp.filesystem
version
.Dv 1.0.0
interface.
Providers expose opaque object handles and resolve names relative to delegated
directory handles.
Backing namespace descriptors remain confined to the provider.
.Pp
The
.Fn filesystemcmp_open
function opens the channel injected under the consumer manifest's local
.Fa component
name.
Passing
.Dv NULL
uses
.Ev FILESYSTEMCMP ,
which
.Xr serviced 8
sets from the successfully injected manifest-local component name.
With no selector, the conventional
.Ql filesystem
name is used.
The variable is only a lookup key into the sealed bootstrap descriptor and
contains no descriptor authority.
The library never names, discovers, or falls back to a concrete provider;
.Xr serviced 8
resolves the requested interface and version before execution.
This permits alternative providers to implement the same versioned protocol
without changing application code.
.Pp
Names are resolved relative to opaque directory handles; absolute path
resolution is never delegated to the client.
Handles carry generations so stale close, lookup, or I/O requests fail closed.
Typed calls cover feature negotiation, root acquisition, lookup, open,
create, bounded positional I/O, stat, unlink, rename, and handle close.
Client-side validation rejects absolute or multi-component names, dot
components, oversized inline I/O, and unknown flag bits before transport.
Provider errors return
.Li -1
and set
.Va errno .
Typed operations are synchronous and complete request/reply exchanges are
serialized within the library.
Fork handlers quiesce an in-flight exchange and leave the client lock usable
in both parent and child.
The descriptor returned by
.Fn filesystemcmp_open
is close-on-exec and owned by the caller.
Bulk I/O may use
.Xr libshmring 3 .
.Pp
The
.Ql filesystemcmp
DTrace provider exposes component-open, message-send, message-receive, and
message-reject probes.
Provider daemons audit authorization, namespace mutation, and denied
resolution decisions through OpenBSM.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr libservice 3 ,
.Xr libshmring 3
